Split sum-type AST nodes into per-variant nodes

Each variant of Term, TypeExpr, PredExpr, FuncExpr, IfAtom, ThenAtom and
Stmt now lives in the arena under its own typed id (VarTermId,
EqualAtomId, ...). The generic id (TermId etc.) remains as a
variant-agnostic handle; ast.term(id) dispatches on the node
discriminant and returns an enum whose variants wrap the specific ids.
Variant ids convert back to the generic id via From.

Equal and Pred atoms are shared between IfAtom and ThenAtom: EqualAtomId
and PredAtomId can appear under either, with the enclosing
IfStmt/ThenStmt recording which.
